IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, s 183 -- circulation of members' resolutions and statements.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Percentages are tested by integer comparison (100 times the part against the percentage times the whole).
-- Section 184A (written means) is a later cluster: whether a resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under it is an input here.

§ `Section 183(2): the number of members needed for a requisition`

-- (2): "The number of members necessary for a requisition under subsection (1) is -- (a) any number of members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights ...; or (b) not less than 100 members
-- holding shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of not less than $500." A closed definition of "the number": JUST FALSE when neither limb holds (F-34).
-- src:16408 | (2) The number of members necessary for a requisition under
-- src:16409 | subsection (1) is —
-- src:16411 | (a) any number of members representing not less than 5% of
-- src:16412 | the total voting rights of all the members having at the date
-- src:16417 | of the requisition a right to vote at the meeting to which the
-- src:16418 | requisition relates; or
-- src:16420 | (b) not less than 100 members holding shares in the company
-- src:16421 | on which there has been paid up an average sum, per
-- src:16422 | member, of not less than $500.
@ref s 183(2) (src:16408-16422)
GIVEN `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having at the date of the requisition a right to vote at the meeting to which the requisition relates` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of requisitionists who hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the total sum paid up on the shares the requisitionists hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(2) the requisition is by the number of members the subsection specifies` MEANS
    IF    (`the total voting rights of all the members having at the date of the requisition a right to vote at the meeting to which the requisition relates` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having at the date of the requisition a right to vote at the meeting to which the requisition relates`)
       OR (`the number of requisitionists who hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100 AND `the total sum paid up on the shares the requisitionists hold` AT LEAST 500 TIMES `the number of requisitionists who hold shares in the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The number of members necessary for a requisition under subsection (1) is -- (a) any number of members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights ...; or (b) not less than 100 members holding shares ... an average sum, per member, of not less than $500" (a closed definition of the number; F-34)

§ `Section 183(4) and (4A): the conditions on which the company is bound`

-- (4): "Subject to subsection (4A), a company is not bound under this section to give notice of any resolution or to circulate any statement unless -- (a) a copy of the requisition signed by the requisitionists,
-- or 2 or more copies which between them contain the signatures of all the requisitionists, is deposited at the registered office of the company -- (i) in the case of a requisition requiring notice of a resolution --
-- not less than 6 weeks before the meeting; and (ii) in the case of any other requisition -- not less than one week before the meeting; and (b) there is deposited or tendered with the requisition a sum reasonably
-- sufficient to meet the company's expenses". An "unless" list closes the gate: JUST FALSE when it is not met (F-35); NOTHING for a resolution proposed to be passed by written means, which (4A) governs.
-- "but if, after a copy of a requisition requiring notice of a resolution has been deposited at the registered office of the company, an annual general meeting is called for a date 6 weeks or less after the
-- copy has been deposited, the copy though not deposited within the time required by this subsection is deemed to have been properly deposited": the date of the meeting is at most 6 weeks after the day of deposit (F-36).
-- src:16456 | (4) Subject to subsection (4A), a company is not bound under this
-- src:16457 | section to give notice of any resolution or to circulate any statement
-- src:16458 | unless —
-- src:16463 | (a) a copy of the requisition signed by the requisitionists,
-- src:16464 | or 2 or more copies which between them contain the
-- src:16465 | signatures of all the requisitionists, is deposited at the
-- src:16466 | registered office of the company —
-- src:16468 | (i) in the case of a requisition requiring notice of a
-- src:16469 | resolution — not less than 6 weeks before the
-- src:16470 | meeting; and
-- src:16472 | (ii) in the case of any other requisition — not less than
-- src:16473 | one week before the meeting; and
-- src:16475 | (b) there is deposited or tendered with the requisition a sum
-- src:16476 | reasonably sufficient to meet the company’s expenses in
-- src:16477 | giving effect thereto,
-- src:16479 | but if, after a copy of a requisition requiring notice of a resolution has
-- src:16480 | been deposited at the registered office of the company, an annual
-- src:16481 | general meeting is called for a date 6 weeks or less after the copy has
-- src:16482 | been deposited, the copy though not deposited within the time
-- src:16483 | required by this subsection is deemed to have been properly deposited
-- src:16484 | for the purposes thereof.
@ref s 183(4) (src:16456-16484)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition requires notice of a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the requisition signed by the requisitionists, or 2 or more copies which between them contain the signatures of all the requisitionists, is deposited at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy was deposited` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `an annual general meeting was called after the copy was deposited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses in giving effect to the requisition is deposited or tendered with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(4) the conditions on which the company is bound to give notice or to circulate are met` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsection (4A)" -- for a resolution proposed to be passed by written means, subsection (4A) governs
    ELSE (IF    `a copy of the requisition signed by the requisitionists, or 2 or more copies which between them contain the signatures of all the requisitionists, is deposited at the registered office of the company`
             AND (   (IF `the requisition requires notice of a resolution`
                      THEN `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the copy was deposited` `the date of the meeting` 6 Weeks
                      ELSE `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the copy was deposited` `the date of the meeting` 1 Weeks)
                  OR (`the requisition requires notice of a resolution` AND `an annual general meeting was called after the copy was deposited` AND `the date of the meeting` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the copy was deposited` 6 Weeks))
             AND `a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses in giving effect to the requisition is deposited or tendered with it`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is not bound under this section to give notice of any resolution or to circulate any statement unless -- (a) ...; and (b) ..." (an "unless" list read as closing the gate; F-35)

-- src:16486 | (4A) A company is not bound under this section to give notice of
-- src:16487 | any resolution which is proposed to be passed by written means under
-- src:16488 | section 184A, or to circulate any statement relating thereto, unless —
-- src:16490 | (a) the requisition setting out the text of the resolution and the
-- src:16491 | statement is received by a director of the company in
-- src:16492 | legible form or a permitted alternative form; and
-- src:16494 | (b) the notice states that formal agreement to the resolution is
-- src:16495 | sought under section 184A.
@ref s 183(4A) (src:16486-16495)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition setting out the text of the resolution and the statement is received by a director of the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that formal agreement to the resolution is sought under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(4A) the conditions on which the company is bound to give notice or to circulate are met` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company is not bound under this section to give notice of any resolution which is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A" -- any other resolution is for subsection (4)
    ELSE (IF `the requisition setting out the text of the resolution and the statement is received by a director of the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form` AND `the notice states that formal agreement to the resolution is sought under section 184A`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is not bound ... unless -- (a) the requisition ... is received by a director ... in legible form or a permitted alternative form; and (b) the notice states that formal agreement to the resolution is sought under section 184A" (F-35)

§ `Section 183(1): the duty to give notice and to circulate`

-- (1)(a): "a company must on the requisition of such number of members of the company as is specified in subsection (2) and, unless the company otherwise resolves, at the expense of the requisitionists --
-- (a) give to members of the company entitled to receive notice of the next annual general meeting notice of any resolution which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at that meeting or (if the resolution
-- is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A) for which agreement is sought". The three answers below are the results of subsections (2), (4) and (4A).
-- src:16390 | 183.—(1) Subject to this section, a company must on the
-- src:16391 | requisition of such number of members of the company as is
-- src:16392 | specified in subsection (2) and, unless the company otherwise
-- src:16393 | resolves, at the expense of the requisitionists —
-- src:16395 | (a) give to members of the company entitled to receive notice
-- src:16396 | of the next annual general meeting notice of any resolution
-- src:16397 | which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved
-- src:16398 | at that meeting or (if the resolution is proposed to be passed
-- src:16399 | by written means under section 184A) for which
-- src:16400 | agreement is sought; and
@ref s 183(1)(a) (src:16390-16400)
GIVEN `the answer under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (4A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at the next annual general meeting or, if proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A, agreement to it is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(1)(a) the company must give members notice of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the answer under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the answer under subsection (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer under subsection (4A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the resolution may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at the next annual general meeting or, if proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A, agreement to it is sought`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company must on the requisition of such number of members ... as is specified in subsection (2) ... give to members ... notice of any resolution which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved" read with "a company is not bound under this section ... unless" (a duty's own question; a gate failed)

-- (1)(b): "circulate to members entitled to have notice of any general meeting sent to them any statement of not more than 1,000 words with respect to the matter referred to in any proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at that meeting".
-- src:16402 | (b) circulate to members entitled to have notice of any general
-- src:16403 | meeting sent to them any statement of not more than
-- src:16404 | 1,000 words with respect to the matter referred to in any
-- src:16405 | proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at that
-- src:16406 | meeting.
@ref s 183(1)(b) (src:16402-16406)
GIVEN `the answer under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (4A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of words in the statement` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement is with respect to the matter referred to in a proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(1)(b) the company must circulate the statement to members` MEANS
    IF    `the answer under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the answer under subsection (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer under subsection (4A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND `the number of words in the statement` AT MOST 1000
      AND `the statement is with respect to the matter referred to in a proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at the meeting`
      AND (NOT (`the answer under subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "circulate ... any statement of not more than 1,000 words with respect to the matter referred to in any proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at that meeting", read with subsections (4) and (5) (a duty's own question; a gate failed)

§ `Section 183(3) to (3C): how the notice and the statement are served`

-- (3): "Subject to subsection (3A), notice of a resolution referred to in subsection (1) must be given, and any statement so referred to must be circulated, to members of the company entitled to have notice of the
-- meeting sent to them by serving on each member, in any manner permitted for service of the notice of the meeting, a copy of the resolution and statement."
-- src:16424 | (3) Subject to subsection (3A), notice of a resolution referred to in
-- src:16425 | subsection (1) must be given, and any statement so referred to must be
-- src:16426 | circulated, to members of the company entitled to have notice of the
-- src:16427 | meeting sent to them by serving on each member, in any manner
-- src:16428 | permitted for service of the notice of the meeting, a copy of the
-- src:16429 | resolution and statement.
@ref s 183(3) (src:16424-16429)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the resolution and statement is served on each member entitled to have notice of the meeting sent to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served in a manner permitted for service of the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(3) the notice and statement are served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsection (3A)" -- for a resolution proposed to be passed by written means, subsection (3A) governs
    ELSE (IF `a copy of the resolution and statement is served on each member entitled to have notice of the meeting sent to them` AND `it is served in a manner permitted for service of the notice of the meeting`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notice of a resolution ... must be given, and any statement ... must be circulated, ... by serving on each member, in any manner permitted for service of the notice of the meeting, a copy of the resolution and statement" (a duty's own question)

-- src:16431 | (3A) Where the resolution is proposed to be passed by written
-- src:16432 | means under section 184A, the notice of the resolution and statement
-- src:16433 | must be given and circulated to members of the company entitled to
-- src:16434 | have notice of the meeting sent to them by serving on each
-- src:16435 | member —
-- src:16437 | (a) a copy of the resolution and statement; and
-- src:16439 | (b) a notification that formal agreement to the resolution is
-- src:16440 | being sought under section 184A.
@ref s 183(3A) (src:16431-16440)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the resolution and statement is served on each member entitled to have notice of the meeting sent to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification that formal agreement to the resolution is being sought under section 184A is served on each of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(3A) the notice and statement are served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A" -- any other resolution is for subsection (3)
    ELSE (IF `a copy of the resolution and statement is served on each member entitled to have notice of the meeting sent to them` AND `a notification that formal agreement to the resolution is being sought under section 184A is served on each of them`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice of the resolution and statement must be given and circulated ... by serving on each member -- (a) a copy of the resolution and statement; and (b) a notification that formal agreement to the resolution is being sought" (a duty's own question)

-- src:16442 | (3B) Notice of the resolution must be given to any other member of
-- src:16443 | the company by serving on the member notice of the general effect of
-- src:16444 | the resolution in any manner permitted for giving the member notice
-- src:16445 | of meetings of the company.
@ref s 183(3B) (src:16442-16445)
GIVEN `the member is a member to whom notice of the meeting is not required to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the general effect of the resolution is served on the member in a manner permitted for giving the member notice of meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(3B) notice of the resolution has been given to the other member as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the member is a member to whom notice of the meeting is not required to be sent`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notice of the resolution must be given to any other member of the company" -- a member to whom notice of the meeting is sent is for subsection (3)
    ELSE (IF `notice of the general effect of the resolution is served on the member in a manner permitted for giving the member notice of meetings of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by serving on the member notice of the general effect of the resolution in any manner permitted for giving the member notice of meetings of the company" (a duty's own question)

-- (3C): "Except where the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A, the copy of the resolution mentioned in subsection (3) must be served, or notice of the general effect of the resolution
-- mentioned in subsection (3B) must be given (as the case may be) in the same manner and, so far as practicable, at the same time as notice of the meeting and, where it is not practicable for it to be served or given
-- at that time, it must be served or given as soon as practicable thereafter." No number of days is stated: the test is "as practicable" (F-39), so no regulative rule is written for it.
-- src:16447 | (3C) Except where the resolution is proposed to be passed by
-- src:16448 | written means under section 184A, the copy of the resolution
-- src:16449 | mentioned in subsection (3) must be served, or notice of the general
-- src:16450 | effect of the resolution mentioned in subsection (3B) must be given
-- src:16451 | (as the case may be) in the same manner and, so far as practicable, at
-- src:16452 | the same time as notice of the meeting and, where it is not practicable
-- src:16453 | for it to be served or given at that time, it must be served or given as
-- src:16454 | soon as practicable thereafter.
@ref s 183(3C) (src:16447-16454)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served or given in the same manner as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served or given at the same time as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not practicable to serve or give it at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served or given as soon as practicable thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(3C) the copy or notice is served or given as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except where the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A" -- subsection (3A) governs
    ELSE (IF `it is served or given in the same manner as notice of the meeting` AND (`it is served or given at the same time as notice of the meeting` OR (`it was not practicable to serve or give it at that time` AND `it is served or given as soon as practicable thereafter`))
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be served, or ... given ... in the same manner and, so far as practicable, at the same time as notice of the meeting and, where it is not practicable ..., as soon as practicable thereafter" (a duty's own question; F-39)

§ `Section 183(4B): the date of receipt of the requisition`

-- (4B): "Where the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that the date of its receipt by a company be notified to a specified person, the directors must, without delay after it is first received by a director
-- in legible form or a permitted alternative form, notify that person of the date when it was first so received." "Without delay" is no number of days, so there is no clock to miss (F-40).
-- src:16497 | (4B) Where the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that
-- src:16498 | the date of its receipt by a company be notified to a specified person,
-- src:16499 | the directors must, without delay after it is first received by a director
-- src:16500 | in legible form or a permitted alternative form, notify that person of
-- src:16501 | the date when it was first so received.
@ref s 183(4B) (src:16497-16501)
GIVEN `the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that the date of its receipt by the company be notified to a specified person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have notified that person of the date when it was first received by a director in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did so without delay after it was first so received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(4B) the directors have complied with the duty to notify the date of receipt` MEANS
    IF NOT `the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that the date of its receipt by the company be notified to a specified person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that the date of its receipt by a company be notified to a specified person, the directors must" (a "where" gate on a duty)
    ELSE (IF `the directors have notified that person of the date when it was first received by a director in legible form or a permitted alternative form` AND `they did so without delay after it was first so received`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must, without delay after it is first received by a director ..., notify that person of the date when it was first so received" (a duty's own question; "without delay" read as an input, F-40)

§ `Section 183(5) and (6)`

-- src:16503 | (5) The company is not bound under this section to circulate any
-- src:16504 | statement if, on the application either of the company or of any other
-- src:16505 | person who claims to be aggrieved, the Court is satisfied that the
-- src:16510 | rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless
-- src:16511 | publicity for defamatory matter and the Court may order the
-- src:16512 | company’s costs on an application under this section to be paid in
-- src:16513 | whole or in part by the requisitionists, even though they are not
-- src:16514 | parties to the application.
@ref s 183(5) (src:16503-16514)
GIVEN `the company or a person who claims to be aggrieved has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(5) the company is not bound to circulate the statement` MEANS
    IF `the company or a person who claims to be aggrieved has applied to the Court` AND `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is not bound under this section to circulate any statement if, on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter" (a bar whose gate failed: the bar does not apply on these facts)

-- "the Court may order the company's costs on an application under this section to be paid in whole or in part by the requisitionists, even though they are not parties to the application": a power gated "on an application under this section" -- an
-- "on application" gate on a "may", so JUST FALSE when there is no application (periods ruling (b); split site (ii), F-37).
@ref s 183(5) (src:16503-16514)
GIVEN `the costs are those of an application under section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(5) the Court may order the requisitionists to pay the company's costs of the application in whole or in part` MEANS
    IF `the costs are those of an application under section 183`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may order the company's costs on an application under this section to be paid in whole or in part by the requisitionists, even though they are not parties to the application" (an "on application" gate on a "may": periods ruling (b); split site (ii), F-37)

-- src:16516 | (6) Despite anything in the company’s constitution, the business
-- src:16517 | which may be dealt with at an annual general meeting includes any
-- src:16518 | resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section,
-- src:16519 | and for the purposes of this subsection notice is deemed to have been
-- src:16520 | so given despite the accidental omission, in giving it, of one or more
-- src:16521 | members.
@ref s 183(6) (src:16516-16521)
GIVEN `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(6) the resolution is business that may be dealt with at the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with section 183`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the business which may be dealt with at an annual general meeting includes any resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section" (a list that is not closed)

@ref s 183(6) (src:16516-16521)
GIVEN `the notice was otherwise given in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more members were omitted from it by accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(6) notice is deemed to have been given despite the accidental omission` MEANS
    IF `the notice was otherwise given in accordance with section 183` AND `one or more members were omitted from it by accident`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice is deemed to have been so given despite the accidental omission, in giving it, of one or more members" -- an omission that was not accidental is outside the deeming (F-38)

§ `Section 183(7) and (8): the offence and the meaning of legible form`

-- src:16525 | (7) In the event of any default in complying with this section, the
-- src:16526 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:16527 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:16528 | exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 183(7) (src:16525-16528)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `there is a default in complying with section 183` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "In the event of any default in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 183(7) (src:16525-16528)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 183(7) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 183(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with section 183` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000; no imprisonment; no default penalty stated
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (8): "something is 'in legible form or a permitted alternative form' if, and only if, it is sent or otherwise supplied -- (a) in a form (such as a paper document) that is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied and does
-- not change form during that process; or (b) in another form that -- (i) is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company; and
-- (ii) is such that documents sent or supplied in that form can (where particular conditions are met) be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form."
-- src:16530 | (8) For the purposes of this section, something is “in legible form or
-- src:16531 | a permitted alternative form” if, and only if, it is sent or otherwise
-- src:16532 | supplied —
-- src:16534 | (a) in a form (such as a paper document) that is legible before
-- src:16535 | being sent or otherwise supplied and does not change form
-- src:16536 | during that process; or
-- src:16538 | (b) in another form that —
-- src:16540 | (i) is currently agreed between the company and the
-- src:16541 | person as a form in which the thing may be sent or
-- src:16542 | otherwise supplied to the company; and
-- src:16544 | (ii) is such that documents sent or supplied in that form
-- src:16545 | can (where particular conditions are met) be received
-- src:16546 | in legible form or be made legible following receipt
-- src:16547 | in non‑legible form.
@ref s 183(8) (src:16530-16547)
GIVEN `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing does not change form during that process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(8) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` MEANS
    IF    (`the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` AND `the thing does not change form during that process`)
       OR (`the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` AND `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "something is 'in legible form or a permitted alternative form' if, and only if, it is sent or otherwise supplied -- (a) ...; or (b) ..." (an "if, and only if" definition)

§ `Regulative rules of s 183`

DECLARE `s 183 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 183(1)(a) give members notice of the resolution`
    `s 183(1)(b) circulate the statement to members`
    `s 183(4B) notify the specified person of the date of receipt`

-- (1)(a) and (1)(b): the company's duties. The text states no time limit and no consequence for either (the offence in (7) is a separate provision), so no trace can show them breached.
-- src:16390 | 183.—(1) Subject to this section, a company must on the
-- src:16391 | requisition of such number of members of the company as is
-- src:16392 | specified in subsection (2) and, unless the company otherwise
-- src:16393 | resolves, at the expense of the requisitionists —
-- src:16395 | (a) give to members of the company entitled to receive notice
-- src:16396 | of the next annual general meeting notice of any resolution
-- src:16397 | which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved
-- src:16398 | at that meeting or (if the resolution is proposed to be passed
-- src:16399 | by written means under section 184A) for which
-- src:16400 | agreement is sought; and
@ref s 183(1)(a) (src:16390-16400)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 183 act`
`s 183(1)(a) the company must give members notice of the resolution (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 183(1)(a) give members notice of the resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 183(1)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give members notice of the resolution" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:16402 | (b) circulate to members entitled to have notice of any general
-- src:16403 | meeting sent to them any statement of not more than
-- src:16404 | 1,000 words with respect to the matter referred to in any
-- src:16405 | proposed resolution or the business to be dealt with at that
-- src:16406 | meeting.
@ref s 183(1)(b) (src:16402-16406)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 183 act`
`s 183(1)(b) the company must circulate the statement to members (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 183(1)(b) circulate the statement to members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 183(1)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not circulate the statement to members" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:16497 | (4B) Where the requisition under subsection (4A)(a) requests that
-- src:16498 | the date of its receipt by a company be notified to a specified person,
-- src:16499 | the directors must, without delay after it is first received by a director
-- src:16500 | in legible form or a permitted alternative form, notify that person of
-- src:16501 | the date when it was first so received.
@ref s 183(4B) (src:16497-16501)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 183 act`
`s 183(4B) the directors must notify the specified person of the date of receipt (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 183(4B) notify the specified person of the date of receipt`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 183(4B) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not notify the specified person of the date when the requisition was first received" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
